From 0388652d1b6f970a18c0b8ccaae9d9c79cece3c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taiki Koshino <koshino@sraoss.co.jp>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 12:37:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Fix operator precedence in parse_wd_node_function_json
 NodeIdList write.

In src/watchdog/wd_json_data.c parse_wd_node_function_json(), the loop
body wrote

    *node_id_set[i] = value->u.array.values[i]->u.integer;

which by C precedence parses as *(node_id_set[i]). node_id_set is an
int ** that aliases the caller's &node_id_list pointer. For i == 0 the
write happens to land on the palloc'd destination buffer; for i >= 1 the
indexing walks sizeof(int*) * i bytes past the int ** parameter into
adjacent memory, dereferences the resulting garbage pointer, and stores
a peer-controlled 32-bit integer there.

Add the missing parentheses so the subscript applies to the dereferenced
array: (*node_id_set)[i] = ...

This is almost certainly the original intent - the single-node
failover path (the common production case) hits only i == 0 and so the
bug has not been observed in normal operation. Any NodeIdList of length
two or more immediately fires the misbehaviour.

Reported-by: Emond Papegaaij <emond.papegaaij@topicus.nl>
Reported-by: Claude
Author: Bo Peng <pengbo@sraoss.co.jp>
CVE-2026-92867
Backpatch-through: v4.3
---
 src/watchdog/wd_json_data.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/watchdog/wd_json_data.c b/src/watchdog/wd_json_data.c
index 26ebd4b5e..41ac92e7c 100644
--- a/src/watchdog/wd_json_data.c
+++ b/src/watchdog/wd_json_data.c
@@ -857,7 +857,7 @@ parse_wd_node_function_json(char *json_data, int data_len, char **func_name, int
 	*node_id_set = palloc(sizeof(int) * node_count);
 	for (i = 0; i < node_count; i++)
 	{
-		*node_id_set[i] = value->u.array.values[i]->u.integer;
+		(*node_id_set)[i] = value->u.array.values[i]->u.integer;
 	}
 	json_value_free(root);
 	return true;
